{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1250177-anything-good-about-lunars","id":1250177,"title":"Anything good about Lunars?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-08-30T22:47:07-07:00","id":1250177,"title":"Anything good about Lunars?","content":"Well, not so long time ago there was discussion about Lunars and their flaws as a splat. Now let's carb the criticism. What is GOOD about Lunars? Is there anything that make them awesome for you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T23:07:42-07:00","id":1250180,"title":"","content":"they let me eat people without getting creeped-out stares from my fellow players","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T23:23:11-07:00","id":1250181,"title":"","content":"BEAST MODE!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T23:49:01-07:00","id":1250187,"title":"","content":"Everything that is visceral*. Everything that burns with rage. Their role as the monsters fighting the corrupt order and acting as the counter-balancing virtue, flipping the tables on expectations and all.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*It is very hard to beat kaijuu for visceral impact and appeal.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-31T02:12:28-07:00","id":1250206,"title":"","content":"They're very diverse; collectively they exhibit a lot of the behaviour of an antagonist splat without it being something you should expect of this particular Lunar. It feels like they're the splat that the Anathema label matters most to - it's easy for Solars to basically shrug it off as &quot;the Dragon-Blooded just jealous of my power&quot; but Lunars are unwholesome enough that they really have to stop and tell people they don't want to hurt them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-31T04:24:59-07:00","id":1250225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1250177-anything-good-about-lunars?p=1250206#post1250206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're very diverse; collectively they exhibit a lot of the behaviour of an antagonist splat without it being something you should expect of this particular Lunar. It feels like they're the splat that the Anathema label matters most to - it's easy for Solars to basically shrug it off as &quot;the Dragon-Blooded just jealous of my power&quot; but Lunars are unwholesome enough that they really have to stop and tell people they don't want to hurt them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ^ Basically this. They're edgy enough to be interesting, but not so edgy as to make me self-conscious about playing them (cough Infernals cough).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-31T06:36:49-07:00","id":1250237,"title":"","content":"Generally speaking, your power isn't &quot;succeed at stealth&quot; but rather &quot;turn into a stealthy animal.&quot; It's not &quot;see in the dark,&quot; it's &quot;use echolocation.&quot; It's not &quot;intimidate people really well&quot;, it's &quot;become a giant ugly monster-beast which is very intimidating.&quot;<br /> <br /> I generally therefore, find their powers more fun to play with, because they involve more thought, but also allow you to be more creative.<br /> But they're easier to use than Sidereals.<br /> <br /> Also, their powers look cool and visceral. And you can rip out a guy's heart and gain his power. Which is cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-31-2018, 10:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-31T08:38:21-07:00","id":1250256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1250177-anything-good-about-lunars?p=1250206#post1250206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're very diverse; collectively they exhibit a lot of the behaviour of an antagonist splat without it being something you should expect of this particular Lunar. It feels like they're the splat that the Anathema label matters most to - it's easy for Solars to basically shrug it off as &quot;the Dragon-Blooded just jealous of my power&quot; but Lunars are unwholesome enough that they really have to stop and tell people they don't want to hurt them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like Japanese youkai.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-31T09:08:52-07:00","id":1250258,"title":"","content":"You get to play Erik &quot;Killmonger&quot; Stevens and <i>win</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-31T13:49:51-07:00","id":1250316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1250177-anything-good-about-lunars#post1250177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, not so long time ago there was discussion about Lunars and their flaws as a splat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to ask which one specifically out of sincere curiosity, and a genuine desire to place this topic into context.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is GOOD about Lunars? Is there anything that make them awesome for you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean essentially and from the beginning, at the moment, or things that I'm anticipating in the final product of this Edition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-31T18:49:20-07:00","id":1250368,"title":"","content":"I am looking forward to the shapeshifting, honestly. And seeing what the crafting and other thinky charms are like this time around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-31T19:38:53-07:00","id":1250378,"title":"","content":"They are the main splat for attribute excellence.<br /> The 'jack of all trades' is rather maligned when it comes to building Exalted characters but in the moment, being the only character who can reliably do something because you can boost your attribute is rather satisfying. While they are not alone in that Alchemicals had slots and installation costs and Infernals had to deal with problems like a Yozi would. The idea is not that you aspire to be an all-rounder who excells at nothing so much as when you encounter something outside your expertise you just shrug and do it anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T02:24:09-07:00","id":1250421,"title":"","content":"That also makes them easier for the ST to deal with, tbh. I can rely on Lunar players to be able to do something in every situation, whereas Solars tend to be overwhelming in some areas and not much above human in others.<br /> <br /> Another thing I really like about Lunars is how easy it is to make an iconic and striking character. All you have to do is pick a cool animal, and you're basically two-thirds of the way there. You can derive personality, powers, etc, from that.<br /> I mean, hopefully people can think of cool characters anyway, but sometimes they can't. Being a Solar lets you play a cool character if you already have a cool character, but doesn't give you much inspiration. You have to find that elsewhere. And so I find about half of Solars are pretty cool characters, and the other half are a bit bland, tbh.<br /> <br /> That's not to crap on Solars. They have their useful role in games. If you have a good concept, Solars will probably allow you to play it in a rather more pure way.<br /> But with Lunars thinking of a very striking and iconic character is easier, because you pick a totem and it gives you a lot of ideas for personality, powers, maybe even background.<br /> <br /> Back in 2nd ed, when people were constantly whining about Lunars on forums, there was quite a few people who said Lunars shouldn't have animal associations, but be Prototype-style shapeshifters. I'm glad the devs have instead decided to lean in to the Totems, making it easier to get powers appropriate to your Totem (with the Totemic keyword). It's just much easier to make an iconic character that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 09-01-2018, 05:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T03:15:19-07:00","id":1250425,"title":"","content":"They're pretty great really.<br /> <br /> Use shapeshifting to take animal forms and gain massive advantages to travel, stealth, survival and perception.<br /> <br /> Steal human forms to infiltrate society and redefine yourself to take any role you wish.<br /> <br /> Apply raw might and cleverness to achieve masterful heroic feats, then when you need to really pull out the stops, use clever attribute stunts or powerful transformative forms to really push your advantages to the limit.<br /> <br /> Draw on a raw, primal, transformative nature only the Lunars have to form unique magical bonds with a world full a spirits and wild, untamed forces.<br /> <br /> Specialize your character's set of capabilities along fresh new lines which are different to the shape of specialisation under any tree the 25 Abilities can encompass, but not inferior as a form of specialization.<br /> <br /> (Parenthetically, to launch into the history, they've been ill served by first changing direction from Fair Folk allies to barbarian heroes, then by two successive iterations of barbarian ideology which the playerbase rejected (fairly or not!). The first, Silver Pact, rejected as luddite and self sabotaging. The second, Thousand Streams, actively addressing those feelings, then rejected as inadequate, since it was pushing against the need for mortals to receive ultra magical-technology and leadership from singular golden heroes, in an edition which increasingly focused on the only thing able to save the world and actually matter being ultra magical-technology and leadership from singular golden heroes! Then once they were a &quot;failure&quot; they were up for grabs for people to argue again about why they were bad and needed to be redefined along some persons vision! But I think the base of what they are need not be weak or uninteresting, or in need of total overhaul or replacement or reimagining.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T12:48:30-07:00","id":1250517,"title":"","content":"Good Lunar things from my past Lunar gaming experience:<br /> <br /> 1. Everybody can participate in sneaky/stealthy infiltration scenes.If they can't, they're just like, &quot;Hang on a sec while I go hunt a mouse.&quot;<br /> <br /> 2. Turn into a big monster and SMASH!<br /> <br /> 3. So much delicious past life relationship angst.<br /> <br /> 4. PCs riding on other PCs, sitting as birds on other PCs' heads, or getting carried in other PCs pockets NEVER stops being delightful. Like, you'd think it'd eventually get old, but nope.<br /> <br /> 5.As an ST, players don't just casually murder the big neat monster you spent all night statting up on Tuesday like Solars. No, they look at it and their eyes sparkle like Pokemon players who just found something Legendary. They fight over who gets to take it's shape. Sometimes they use talking to animals charms to make friends with it.<br /> <br /> 6. Even more yummy queer drama than other Exalts. Lunars tend to bring out their player's inner freak. USUALLY in a good way...<br /> <br /> 7. Pranking random mortals by being a talking dog/horse/whatever. Alternately, pretending to be local divinities. Once had an Appearance Lunar show up in Marukan and be like, &quot;It is I, Hipparkes, God of Horses! Bring me offerings of hay and your finest jewelry to adorn my incomparable mane!&quot;<br /> <br /> 8. There's always that guy who flies over the enemy as a sparrow and then turns into a whale/tyrant lizard for an epic bodyslam. There's always that guy who flies up a Wyld Hunter's nose as a fly and then turns into a hedgehog. There's occasionally that guy you have to talk out of his Candiru totem former Guild slave courtesan concept.The first two are worth dealing with the third.<br /> <br /> 9. Every time somebody makes a Sailor Moon reference.<br /> <br /> 10. Guerilla warfare!<br /> <br /> 11. Charm-allowed Dawn vs Full Moon drinking contests.<br /> <br /> 12. Using ridiculous strength charm shenanigans combined with &quot;anything you can hold in one hand&quot; elsewhere pickpocketing charms to put whole ships, warstriders, and on one notable occasion the ENTIRE CITY OF LOOKSHY in your pocket.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T16:38:52-07:00","id":1250566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1250177-anything-good-about-lunars?p=1250517#post1250517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good Lunar things from my past Lunar gaming experience:<br /> <br /> <br /> 10. Guerilla warfare!</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't you mean....<br /> <br /> ......<br /> <br /> <br /> .....Ok, I won't go there. I'm sure we're all better than that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T17:50:05-07:00","id":1250577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1250177-anything-good-about-lunars?p=1250566#post1250566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't you mean....<br /> <br /> ......<br /> <br /> <br /> .....Ok, I won't go there. I'm sure we're all better than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I go to all this effort to set you up for a pun, and you don't go there?! That set up was prime, mate! Don't chimp out on me!<br /> <br /> Quit monkeying around and being coy. Between the two of us we could orangutan of Lunar themed Ape-puns!<br /> <br /> &quot;Better than that?&quot; Mandrill it into your head-I will never stop making bad primate puns.<br /> <br /> ... although this conversation does remind me of another fun Lunar memory, so...<br /> <br /> 13. Players spontaneously all busting out into &quot;RAAAAAKSI! YOU DON'T HAVE TO PUT OUT A RED LIGHT!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T20:19:33-07:00","id":1250622,"title":"","content":"&quot;It's not Gorilla! It's <i>Gorilla gorilla gorilla</i>!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T20:21:01-07:00","id":1250623,"title":"","content":"They are one of two Exalted societies in Creation that have millennia-old elders that have passed down lived experience to the newly Exalted. The Sidereals have their particular flavor, which is wrapped up in Yu-Shan, with the gods and their duties. The Lunars, however, learn how to survive a hostile world - age itself being a worthy accomplishment - from the elders who have braved horrors and wonders, temptations and trials.<br /> <br /> Exploring some of this Lunar narrative space in first-person character writeups, ala Castebooks, was a fun way for me to geek out about Exalted while my group was busy '<i>having lives</i>' and '<i>doing things</i>'. I'm being sarcastic for flavor. Anyway, if that's your jam, check out the link in my signature - lots of Lunar love down there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}